#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitor a job {#monitor-a-job}"
msgstr "I-monitor ang isang job {#monitor-a-job}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use these methods to check the status of your submitted jobs, retrieve results, and view details related to the job and its execution.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang mga method na ito para suriin ang status ng iyong mga isinumiteng job, kunin ang mga resulta, at tingnan ang mga detalye na kaugnay ng job at ng pagpapatakbo nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Monitor a job with Qiskit\">\n"
"        The job instance provides several methods for monitoring:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Monitor a job with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Nagbibigay ang job instance ng ilang method para sa pagsubaybay:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        | Method | Description |\n"
"        | --- | --- |\n"
"        | `job.status()` | Check the current job status |\n"
"        | `job.job_id()` | Get the unique job identifier |\n"
"        | `job.result()` | Retrieve job results (blocking call until complete) |\n"
"        | `job.wait_for_final_state()` | Block until the job reaches a terminal state |\n"
msgstr ""
"        | Method | Description |\n"
"        | --- | --- |\n"
"        | `job.status()` | Check the current job status |\n"
"        | `job.job_id()` | Get the unique job identifier |\n"
"        | `job.result()` | Retrieve job results (blocking call until complete) |\n"
"        | `job.wait_for_final_state()` | Block until the job reaches a terminal state |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Monitor a job on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Navigate to the [Workloads page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) and check the Status column. Your job status appears as one of the following:\n"
"        - **Pending**: Job is waiting to run on a QPU\n"
"        - **In progress**: Job is currently executing\n"
"        - **Completed**: Job finished successfully\n"
"        - **Failed**: Job encountered an error\n"
"        - **Canceled**: User canceled the job\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Monitor a job on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Pumunta sa [Workloads page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) at tingnan ang Status column. Ang status ng iyong job ay makikita bilang isa sa mga sumusunod:\n"
"        - **Pending**: Job is waiting to run on a QPU\n"
"        - **In progress**: Job is currently executing\n"
"        - **Completed**: Job finished successfully\n"
"        - **Failed**: Job encountered an error\n"
"        - **Canceled**: User canceled the job\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        Click on the job name or row to open the detailed view, where you can see information such as the results and any error messages.\n"
msgstr "        I-click ang job name o row para buksan ang detailed view, kung saan makikita mo ang impormasyon tulad ng mga resulta at anumang mga error message.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why a job stays \"In progress\" {#why-a-job-stays-in-progress}"
msgstr "Bakit nananatiling \"In progress\" ang isang job {#why-a-job-stays-in-progress}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might notice that a job (using either job mode or batch mode) you expect to take only a few seconds stays in the **In progress** status (called `RUNNING` in Qiskit) for much longer. This is normal, and it does not mean the job is consuming that entire time as usage. It happens because of how jobs are scheduled onto a QPU:\n"
msgstr "Mapapansin mo na ang isang job (gamit man ang job mode o batch mode) na inaasahan mong ilang segundo lang ang tatagal ay nananatili sa **In progress** status (tinatawag na `RUNNING` sa Qiskit) nang mas matagal. Normal ito, at hindi ito nangangahulugan na ginagamit ng job ang buong oras na iyon bilang usage. Nangyayari ito dahil sa kung paano naka-iskedyul ang mga job papunta sa isang QPU:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job requires classical pre-processing before it can run on the QPU. A job moves to **In progress** (`RUNNING`) as soon as this classical processing begins — not when it starts executing on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Kailangan ng bawat job ng classical pre-processing bago ito makapagpatakbo sa QPU. Ang isang job ay lumilipat sa **In progress** (`RUNNING`) sa sandaling magsimula ang classical processing na ito — hindi kapag nagsisimula itong mag-execute sa QPU.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most of this classical processing runs in parallel, so multiple jobs can be **In progress** at the same time.\n"
msgstr "Karamihan sa classical processing na ito ay tumatakbo nang parallel, kaya maaaring **In progress** ang maraming job nang sabay-sabay.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, only one job at a time can run on the QPU. When several jobs finish their classical processing and are ready to execute, they must wait their turn for the QPU. This is known as *QPU contention*. When contention is high, a job can remain **In progress** noticeably longer than the few seconds of QPU time it actually needs.\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, isang job lang sa isang pagkakataon ang maaaring tumakbo sa QPU. Kapag natapos na ng ilang job ang kanilang classical processing at handa nang mag-execute, kailangan nilang maghintay ng turno para sa QPU. Ito ay tinatawag na *QPU contention*. Kapag mataas ang contention, maaaring manatiling **In progress** ang isang job nang mas matagal kumpara sa ilang segundong QPU time na talagang kailangan nito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contention can also occur when a system-maintenance task, such as calibration, is running on the QPU. Your job stays **In progress** until the maintenance task completes and the QPU becomes available.\n"
msgstr "Maaari ring mangyari ang contention kapag may tumatakbong system-maintenance task, tulad ng calibration, sa QPU. Mananatiling **In progress** ang iyong job hanggang matapos ang maintenance task at maging available ang QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because of this, the elapsed wall-clock time a job spends **In progress** is not the same as its usage. Both the [estimated usage](/guides/estimate-job-run-time) and the [maximum execution time](/guides/max-execution-time) are based only on the time the QPU is locked to execute your job, and therefore exclude the multi-threaded classical processing described above. A long **In progress** time does not increase your reported usage or cost.\n"
msgstr "Dahil dito, ang naubos na wall-clock time ng isang job habang **In progress** ay hindi katumbas ng usage nito. Ang parehong [estimated usage](/guides/estimate-job-run-time) at [maximum execution time](/guides/max-execution-time) ay batay lamang sa oras na naka-lock ang QPU para i-execute ang iyong job, at dahil dito hindi kasama ang multi-threaded classical processing na inilarawan sa itaas. Ang mahabang **In progress** na oras ay hindi nagpapataas ng iyong naiuulat na usage o gastos.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session mode is different {#session-mode-is-different}"
msgstr "Iba ang session mode {#session-mode-is-different}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preceding behavior applies to [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) and [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode). In [session mode](/guides/execution-modes#session-mode), during the session's active window, the user has exclusive access to the backend and no other jobs can run, including calibration jobs. Therefore, any QPU contention happens only among your own session jobs. In addition, because QPU capacity is reserved for the duration of the session, session usage is measured as the elapsed time while the session remains active, regardless of whether jobs are actively running. See [Workload usage](/guides/estimate-job-run-time#usage) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Ang naunang paguugali ay naaangkop sa [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) at [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode). Sa [session mode](/guides/execution-modes#session-mode), sa panahon ng active window ng session, eksklusibong access lang ang mayroon ang user sa backend at walang ibang job ang maaaring tumakbo, kabilang ang mga calibration job. Dahil dito, ang anumang QPU contention ay nangyayari lamang sa pagitan ng iyong sariling mga session job. Bukod dito, dahil nakareserba ang QPU capacity sa buong tagal ng session, ang session usage ay sinusukat bilang naubos na oras habang aktibo ang session, anuman ang status ng mga tumatakbong job. Tingnan ang [Workload usage](/guides/estimate-job-run-time#usage) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "View remaining usage {#view-remaining-usage}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang natitirang paggamit {#view-remaining-usage}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Track how much of your plan's usage quota remains.\n"
msgstr "Subaybayan kung gaano karami ang natitira sa usage quota ng iyong plano.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Check usage with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Use the `service.usage()` method to get usage information for your current active instance.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Check usage with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Gamitin ang `service.usage()` method para makuha ang impormasyon ng usage para sa iyong kasalukuyang active instance.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"View usage on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Navigate to the [Instances page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) and select the tab associated with the plan you want to check. The total time used and total time remaining on your plan is displayed.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"View usage on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Pumunta sa [Instances page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) at piliin ang tab na nauugnay sa plano na gusto mong tingnan. Ipinapakita ang kabuuang oras na ginamit at kabuuang oras na natitira sa iyong plano.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "View job metrics {#view-job-metrics}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang mga metrics ng job {#view-job-metrics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get an overview of your job submissions, including batch and session workload metrics.\n"
msgstr "Kumuha ng overview ng iyong mga pagsumite ng job, kabilang ang batch at session workload metrics.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Get job metrics with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Use the [`service.jobs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#jobs)  method with filters to retrieve information about your submitted jobs, such as how many have been submitted, what their statuses are, and when they were created. The following example retrieves all jobs submitted in the last seven days and calculates the total usage from those jobs.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Get job metrics with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Gamitin ang [`service.jobs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#jobs)  method na may mga filter para makuha ang impormasyon tungkol sa iyong mga isinumiteng job, tulad ng kung ilan ang naisumite, ano ang kanilang status, at kailan sila ginawa. Ang sumusunod na halimbawa ay kumukuha ng lahat ng job na isinumite sa nakaraang pitong araw at kinakalkula ang kabuuang usage mula sa mga job na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"View job metrics on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Navigate to the [Analytics page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/analytics) to see and download data, such as the following:\n"
"        - Total usage\n"
"        - Usage filtered by instance, quantum computer, and user\n"
"        - Count of job, batch, and session workloads\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"View job metrics on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Pumunta sa [Analytics page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/analytics) para makita at ma-download ang data, tulad ng mga sumusunod:\n"
"        - Total usage\n"
"        - Usage filtered by instance, quantum computer, and user\n"
"        - Count of job, batch, and session workloads\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        **Note**: You can only access the Analytics page for accounts that you own or manage.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        **Tandaan**: Maa-access mo lang ang Analytics page para sa mga account na pagmamay-ari mo o pinapamahalaan mo.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve job results at a later time {#retrieve-job-results-at-a-later-time}"
msgstr "Kunin ang mga resulta ng job sa ibang pagkakataon {#retrieve-job-results-at-a-later-time}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can save job IDs and retrieve results later, even after closing your session.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong i-save ang mga job ID at kunin ang mga resulta sa ibang pagkakataon, kahit pagkatapos isara ang iyong session.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Retrieve results with Qiskit\">\n"
"        If you saved the job ID when you submitted the job, use `service.job(<job_id>)` to retrieve it later. If you don't have the job ID, or if you want to retrieve multiple jobs at once (including jobs from retired QPUs), use `service.jobs()` instead, with optional filters.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Retrieve results with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Kung na-save mo ang job ID nang isinumite mo ang job, gamitin ang `service.job(<job_id>)` para kunin ito sa ibang pagkakataon. Kung wala kang job ID, o kung gusto mong kunin ang maraming job nang sabay-sabay (kabilang ang mga job mula sa mga retired QPU), gamitin ang `service.jobs()` sa halip, na may mga opsyonal na filter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        See the [`QiskitRuntimeService.jobs`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#jobs) API documentation for available filters.\n"
msgstr "        Tingnan ang [`QiskitRuntimeService.jobs`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#jobs) API documentation para sa mga available na filter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        This example demonstrates retrieving recent results run on a specific backend.\n"
msgstr "        Ipinapakita ng halimbawang ito ang pagkuha ng mga kamakailang resulta na pinatakbo sa isang partikular na backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Retrieve results on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        1. Go to the [Workloads page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads).\n"
"        2. Use the search or filter options to find your job by name, date, or status.\n"
"        3. Click on the job to view its results and details.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Retrieve results on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        1. Pumunta sa [Workloads page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads).\n"
"        2. Gamitin ang search o filter options para hanapin ang iyong job ayon sa pangalan, petsa, o status.\n"
"        3. I-click ang job para tingnan ang mga resulta at detalye nito.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve backend properties {#retrieve-backend-properties}"
msgstr "Kunin ang mga property ng backend {#retrieve-backend-properties}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Retrieve backend properties with Qiskit\">\n"
"        You can use `job.properties()` to retrieve backend properties, including error rates, at the time of the job execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Retrieve backend properties with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Maaari mong gamitin ang `job.properties()` para kunin ang mga property ng backend, kabilang ang mga error rate, sa oras ng pagpapatakbo ng job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        This example demonstrates how to retrieve backend properties that were current at the time a job was executed, including $T_1$/$T_2$ times and error rates for a specific qubit (0).\n"
msgstr "        Ipinapakita ng halimbawang ito kung paano kunin ang mga property ng backend na kasalukuyan noong pinapatakbo ang isang job, kabilang ang mga $T_1$/$T_2$ na oras at error rate para sa isang partikular na qubit (0).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Deprecated provider packages\">\n"
"            `service.jobs()` also returns jobs run from the deprecated `qiskit-ibm-provider` package. Jobs submitted by the older (also deprecated) `qiskit-ibmq-provider` package are no longer available.\n"
"        </Admonition>\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Retrieve backend properties on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        You can see calibration data for the backend at the time of job execution, as well as at job creation.\n"
"        1. Go to the [Workloads page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads)\n"
"        2. Click a workload to open its Details page\n"
"        3. Under Quantum computer, click View calibration history\n"
"        4. Use the dropdown menu to change from viewing the data \"At job execution start\" to \"At job creation\"\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        <Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mga deprecated na provider package\">\n"
"            Ibinabalik din ng `service.jobs()` ang mga job na pinatakbo mula sa deprecated na `qiskit-ibm-provider` package. Ang mga job na isinumite ng mas lumang (deprecated rin) `qiskit-ibmq-provider` package ay hindi na available.\n"
"        </Admonition>\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Retrieve backend properties on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Makikita mo ang calibration data para sa backend sa oras ng pagpapatakbo ng job, gayundin sa oras ng paggawa ng job.\n"
"        1. Pumunta sa [Workloads page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads)\n"
"        2. I-click ang isang workload para buksan ang Details page nito\n"
"        3. Sa ilalim ng Quantum computer, i-click ang View calibration history\n"
"        4. Gamitin ang dropdown menu para lumipat mula sa pagtingin ng data na \"At job execution start\" patungo sa \"At job creation\"\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "I-cancel ang isang job {#cancel-a-job}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job that is queued or running. Once a job is canceled, it cannot be resumed.\n"
msgstr "Kanselahin ang isang job na naka-queue o tumatakbo. Kapag nakansela na ang isang job, hindi na ito maaaring ipagpatuloy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Cancel with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Use the `job.cancel()` method to cancel a job programmatically.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit\" label=\"Cancel with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Gamitin ang `job.cancel()` method para kanselahin ang isang job nang programmatic.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Cancel on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        1. **From the workloads table**: Click the overflow menu at the end of the row for the workload you want to cancel, and select **Cancel**.\n"
"        2. **From the job details page**: Click on the workload to open its details page, use the **Actions** dropdown at the top, and select **Cancel**.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP\" label=\"Cancel on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        1. **From the workloads table**: I-click ang overflow menu sa dulo ng row para sa workload na gusto mong kanselahin, at piliin ang **Cancel**.\n"
"        2. **From the job details page**: I-click ang workload para buksan ang details page nito, gamitin ang **Actions** dropdown sa itaas, at piliin ang **Cancel**.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

